062 - How Lovely Is Thy Dwelling Place
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 62
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]How lovely [F]is [Dm]Thy dwelling [Bb]place,
[Bb]O Lord [F7]of hosts to [Ab]me!
[F7]The [Gm]tabenacles [F]of Thy [Bb]grace
[Bb]How pleasant, Lord, [F]they [Eb]be!

Verse 2:
[Bb]My thirsty [Dm]soul [F]longs [Dm]ardently,
[Bb]Yea, faints [F7]Thy courts to [Ab]see;
[F7]My [Gm]very heart and [F]flesh cry [Bb]out,
[Bb]O living God, [F]for [Eb]Thee.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Behold [Dm]the sparrow findeth [Cm]out
[Bb]A house [F7]where-in to [Ab]rest;
[F7]The [Gm]swallow also, [F]for herself
[Bb]Provided hath [F]a [Eb]nest.

Verse 4:
[Bb]Ev'n Thine [Dm]own altars, where she [Cm]safe
[Bb]Her young [F]ones [F7]forth [Ab]may bring,
[F7]O [Gm]Thou, [Bb]almighty [F]Lord of [Bb]hosts,
[Bb]Who art my God [F]and [Eb]King.

Verse 5:
[Bb]Blest are [Dm]they in [F]Thy [Dm]house that [Cm]dwell,
[Bb]They ever [F7]give Thee [Ab]praise.
[F7]Blest [Gm]is [Bb]the [Gm]man whose [F]strength Thou [Bb]art,
[Bb]In whose heart are [F]Thy [Eb]ways.
